# Explore the Geometry of Stereographic Attention

Begin with the central surprise: a decreasing kernel need not create tiny weights when its domain is bounded. On a unit sphere, chordal distance never exceeds $2$, so the raw Cauchy score $1/(1+\|q-k\|^2)$ never falls below $1/5$.

