The condition $K_ eta(q,k)\geq	au$ is equivalent to $\|q-k\|^2\leq(	au^{-1}-1)/ eta$. For Euclidean unit vectors, $\|q-k\|^2=2-2\langle q,kangle$, so activity is an inner-product cutoff and therefore a spherical cap. See [spherical cap](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spherical_cap) and [concentration of measure](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concentration_of_measure) for the probabilistic setting.

</details>

## Where to go next

Powered kernels, bandwidth calibration, binomial concentration, normalized top-$k$ error, and universality of positive Cauchy mixtures form a concrete research program. The essential design rule is simple: calculate the geometry-induced kernel floor before claiming threshold sparsity.
